    "turn_text": "know, I don't, you just don't know where to start. I think more than ever I think we need to at least get into a space where we can have dialogues like this. You're never going to have the same opinion as somebody else and I don't think we want that in this country. We want diverse opinions. We want people to be educated on issues and we want as many different thoughts to come to the table. And I think that in order for us to do that we need to create an environment kind of like this where we can talk about that. My husband and I don't agree, trust me. We don't agree on a wide variety of issues, but we're partners and we know that we are in a space where we're just trying to make things better for our family, for our community, and for our country. And so I think that I've always said that when two people get into a room and they talk about what they're for, that's American democracy at its best. And we have to make sure that we preserve the voice of the American people so that Washington is not bulldozing over. our voice that we're able to raise our voice here in the state of Utah and as individuals and do everything we can to promote the values that we have. So I am excited to be here and that's the space that I'm in.",
