  {
    "episode_id": 96001,
    "turn_file": "/shared/3/projects/podcasts/transcriptionQueue/turns/pol_appearance_episodes_interviews/9/6/96001.jsonl",
    "turn_idx": 24,
    "turn_text": "Okay, so I can tell you, we're going to be talking about this, but I can tell you, I think it's important for us to go into spaces that would be seemingly uncomfortable. And then you're going to find yourself in a space where you actually can affect some change and things aren't as bad as you think. For instance, I'm the only person in the Utah delegation that's on the climate solutions caucus. I'm proudly a member of the Climate Solutions Caucus because I think as an individual and as a mom, I have a responsibility to our environment and to what's happening in our, I'm a runner. You know, it doesn't take a rocket science to walk out the door and say, hmm, you know, we've got an issue here and I could either ignore it or I could be part of the solution. Right. That's one thing. So you hear about these things and they've got the media out there that's causing this fight and they make money from seeing people fight each other. When in reality, it's not really like that. So the Climate Solutions Caucus is a bipartisan caucus where I am there with members from both sides of the aisle that are willing to actually have a dialogue on what we can do as individuals to create a placed or at least preserve this beautiful land that we've inherited. The other thing that is important to know, I'm the only Republican in the Congressional Black Caucus, you wouldn't believe the type of relationship we have. As a matter of fact, last election, we actually had a Democrat for the first time in a very, very long time support. outwardly support a Republican. Now, I can tell you that the political parties did not like that at all. They don't. I think that it says something about him as an individual that would be willing to go out and say, you know what, I think it's important for us to have people of color on both sides of the aisle, and it's important for us to make sure that we have women representing us in Washington And he went out on the limb and said, I'm going to support me of love. And I have to tell you that he is one of my best friends. There are people that I would really give my life for that don't always agree with me, but I'm telling you the respect that we have for one another. The media will never portray that or will never show that. So.",
