    "turn_idx": 40,
    "turn_text": "And so those are the things that you can do on a municipal level. And when somebody said, okay, you were able to work that way. Can you bring a little bit of what we do, what you did in your city to Washington, which is why, after a lot of convincing, I decided that I can help my children and certainly help cities, individual cities, by pushing what we can at the local level. When you talked about the solutions, I think that the best solutions and the most effective government is found at the local level because we remove all of the partisanship out of it. So I try and do what I can, which is why I think John is going to be a great member of Congress. He understands what it's like to work on a municipal level. He understands that when Washington takes away the tools that you have, it's harder for you to be able to reply or take care of your constituents. And so we do what we can to make sure that we give our local mayors, our county mayors, our states as much of the tools that they can so that they can take care of the people that they can see.",
