    "turn_file": "/shared/3/projects/podcasts/transcriptionQueue/turns/pol_appearance_episodes_interviews/9/6/96001.jsonl",
    "turn_idx": 53,
    "turn_text": "Being a Utahn and being an American and I think we all have a responsibility outside of ourselves. The world doesn't revolve around us. I try and teach my children that they have to use their gifts and their talents for the betterment of their neighbors, for the betterment of their country. It's important for my kids to not just hear it but to see it and to see that it takes a little bit of sacrifice. We have forgotten in this country how to take care of one another. We've forgotten how to be completely respectful to one another, that we're all Americans, and we all have a responsibility to each other. The reason why I do this, I think it's worth it. Because one, I believe, especially the days where we can actually get something done and make a change, those are good. And as an example to my children and doing everything I can to make this country a little bit better than what we've inherited, it's important to be an example to show them that, okay, mom and dad are out there sacrificing. I have a responsibility too. I can do something too.",
    "speaker_id": "SPEAKER_01",
