    "turn_idx": 113,
    "turn_text": "You know, I think we I really do think we can it takes several things one it takes The ability to, you have to stop ignoring. I get it on my side of the aisle. You have to stop ignoring that there's an issue. And you have to admit that we can do something to solve it. That doesn't hurt any other industry. As a matter of fact, I am pro clean energy. I think it's important for us to explore as much as possible, to allow people to have that space for innovation. If we stifle that, then we're going to be stuck in energy producing ways that We just need to allow people to promote and to find ways that we can support clean energy. That's one way that we can do that. I think Utah is a great place, ground zero for something like that. I think that there are all of the energy producing companies that are out there or industries that are out there can come to the table and be part of that solution. When I talk about innovation, if you think about what we've done in the automobile world, we need to allow people to innovate and grow and get those products to the market at a lower cost.",
    "speaker_id": "SPEAKER_01",
