  {
    "episode_id": 96001,
    "turn_file": "/shared/3/projects/podcasts/transcriptionQueue/turns/pol_appearance_episodes_interviews/9/6/96001.jsonl",
    "turn_idx": 154,
    "turn_text": "Well, I am doing everything I can to fix it. It's a responsibility that I believe I have. So we've sponsored a bill called the RAC Act. And what it does is it allows the dreamers within five years that they could work, have a full-time job, or be enrolled in school full-time, or serve in the military. They cannot have a criminal record, which is a felony. They can't have a felony. And after, if they're able to do that, five years, they can apply for their residency and be able to get their pathway through citizenship. And I can tell you right now, that is something, once they get to, that no one can take away from them. Because if you think about this, there are people out there that don't know another country. They're Americans. You send people off and all of a sudden they're in a country that they don't know. We have to be able to fix this problem that I think Washington created.",
