  {
    "episode_id": 96001,
    "turn_file": "/shared/3/projects/podcasts/transcriptionQueue/turns/pol_appearance_episodes_interviews/9/6/96001.jsonl",
    "turn_idx": 166,
    "turn_text": "What's next for me? I'm so focused on what I'm doing. There's so much to do right now. Again, we have to watch out for cyber security and the breaches that we've had. We've seen it in the financial sector, the SEC, we've seen it at Equifax. I mean, that's, again, my area of jurisdiction, 1.4 million Utahns alone were compromised by Equifax. We've seen that there's a lot of foreign threats out there. I think now more than ever we really do need to concentrate on banding together and looking out for one another. I am, you know, I am who I am. I've seen a lot of the policies work as a mother, work as a mayor, and I'm trying to bring a little bit of that to Washington. I am a free market person. I mean, I believe that free markets have taken more people out of poverty. Well, actually, I don't believe I know free markets have taken more people out of poverty than any other economic system in the history of the world. And I'm trying to do everything I can to promote that. And I think that if we can do that, especially in our in some of our clean energy areas and getting those products out to people, we're going to see a big difference in how people see and treat our environment and protect the beauty of the landscapes that we have, not just in this country, but here in the state of Utah. We have five national parks here. We want people to be able to come and visit and see and enjoy and not have to worry about being outdoors. My job here is to continue to protect my children's future, to continue to protect Utah's interest, what we do here in innovation, allowing you guys to go and make this world move. I mean, just think about the tech industry and what they've done with job creation here, how much further we can go if we have the workforce. So there's so much to do when it comes to education, when it comes to access to credit, when it comes to tax reform, climate solutions. It's something that I think everyone can get on board with and I'm going to do everything I can to leave this world a little bit better than we found it for my children and for your children.",
